# ROS WMS

Warehouse Management System / robot development workspace using **ROS 2 Jazzy**, **C++**, and **Python**.

> This README includes a practical ROS 2 Jazzy developer command reference. The exact CLI commands available on a machine can vary depending on installed ROS 2 packages and CLI extensions.

## Requirements

- Ubuntu 24.04 LTS
- ROS 2 Jazzy Jalisco
- Python 3
- C++17 or newer
- `colcon`
- `rosdep`

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone git@github.com:kofinder/ros_wms.git
cd ros_wms
```

## 2. ROS 2 Environment

Source ROS 2 Jazzy:

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
```

Verify:

```bash
ros2 --help
echo $ROS_DISTRO
echo $ROS_VERSION
echo $ROS_DOMAIN_ID
printenv | grep ROS
```

Expected distribution:

```text
jazzy
```

Optional automatic sourcing:

```bash
echo "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
```

## 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
sudo apt update
rosdep update
rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -r -y
```

## 4. Build Workspace

Build everything:

```bash
colcon build
```

Development build:

```bash
colcon build --symlink-install
```

Build a specific package:

```bash
colcon build --packages-select hello
```

Build multiple packages:

```bash
colcon build --packages-select package1 package2
```

Build up to a package:

```bash
colcon build --packages-up-to hello
```

Clean CMake cache:

```bash
colcon build --cmake-clean-cache
```

Full clean:

```bash
rm -rf build install log
colcon build --symlink-install
```

## 5. Source Workspace

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
```

## 6. Package Commands

```bash
ros2 pkg list
ros2 pkg list | grep hello
ros2 pkg prefix hello
ros2 pkg executables
ros2 pkg executables hello
```

Create a C++ package:

```bash
cd src
ros2 pkg create \
  --build-type ament_cmake \
  --license Apache-2.0 \
  my_cpp_package
```

Create a Python package:

```bash
cd src
ros2 pkg create \
  --build-type ament_python \
  --license Apache-2.0 \
  my_python_package
```

Create with dependencies:

```bash
ros2 pkg create \
  --build-type ament_cmake \
  --dependencies rclcpp std_msgs geometry_msgs \
  robot_controller
```

## 7. Run Nodes

Current project example:

```bash
ros2 run hello publisher
```

General syntax:

```bash
ros2 run <package_name> <executable_name>
```

Examples:

```bash
ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker

ros2 run hello publisher \
  --ros-args \
  -r __node:=wms_publisher

ros2 run hello publisher \
  --ros-args \
  -r __ns:=/robot1

ros2 run hello publisher \
  --ros-args \
  --log-level debug
```

## 8. Node Commands

```bash
ros2 node list
ros2 node info /node_name
```

Example:

```bash
ros2 node info /publisher
```

## 9. Topic Commands

```bash
ros2 topic list
ros2 topic list -t
ros2 topic info /topic_name
ros2 topic info /topic_name --verbose
ros2 topic echo /topic_name
ros2 topic hz /topic_name
ros2 topic bw /topic_name
```

Publish a string:

```bash
ros2 topic pub \
  /topic_name \
  std_msgs/msg/String \
  "{data: 'Hello ROS 2'}"
```

Publish once:

```bash
ros2 topic pub --once \
  /topic_name \
  std_msgs/msg/String \
  "{data: 'Hello ROS 2'}"
```

Publish at 10 Hz:

```bash
ros2 topic pub --rate 10 \
  /topic_name \
  std_msgs/msg/String \
  "{data: 'Hello ROS 2'}"
```

Robot velocity example:

```bash
ros2 topic pub --once \
  /cmd_vel \
  geometry_msgs/msg/Twist \
  "{linear: {x: 0.2}, angular: {z: 0.0}}"
```

## 10. Interface Commands

```bash
ros2 interface list
ros2 interface show std_msgs/msg/String
ros2 interface show geometry_msgs/msg/Twist
ros2 interface show std_srvs/srv/SetBool
ros2 interface show example_interfaces/action/Fibonacci
ros2 interface package geometry_msgs
```

## 11. Service Commands

```bash
ros2 service list
ros2 service list -t
ros2 service type /service_name
ros2 service find std_srvs/srv/Trigger
ros2 service info /service_name
```

Call a service:

```bash
ros2 service call \
  /service_name \
  std_srvs/srv/Trigger
```

Call with request data:

```bash
ros2 service call \
  /set_bool \
  std_srvs/srv/SetBool \
  "{data: true}"
```

## 12. Parameter Commands

```bash
ros2 param list
ros2 param list /node_name
ros2 param get /node_name parameter_name
ros2 param set /node_name parameter_name value
ros2 param describe /node_name parameter_name
ros2 param dump /node_name
```

Save parameters:

```bash
ros2 param dump /node_name > params.yaml
```

Load parameters:

```bash
ros2 param load /node_name params.yaml
```

Pass a parameter:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  -p max_speed:=1.0
```

Use a parameter file:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  --params-file config/params.yaml
```

## 13. Action Commands

```bash
ros2 action list
ros2 action list -t
ros2 action info /action_name
ros2 action type /action_name
```

Send a goal:

```bash
ros2 action send_goal \
  /action_name \
  example_interfaces/action/Fibonacci \
  "{order: 10}"
```

With feedback:

```bash
ros2 action send_goal \
  /action_name \
  example_interfaces/action/Fibonacci \
  "{order: 10}" \
  --feedback
```

## 14. Launch Commands

```bash
ros2 launch <package_name> <launch_file>
```

Example:

```bash
ros2 launch robot_bringup robot.launch.py
```

Show arguments:

```bash
ros2 launch robot_bringup robot.launch.py --show-args
```

Pass arguments:

```bash
ros2 launch robot_bringup robot.launch.py use_sim_time:=true
```

## 15. ROS 2 Bag

```bash
ros2 bag --help
ros2 bag record -a
ros2 bag record /scan /odom /cmd_vel
ros2 bag record -o robot_test /scan /odom /cmd_vel
ros2 bag info robot_test
ros2 bag play robot_test
ros2 bag play --loop robot_test
ros2 bag play --rate 0.5 robot_test
```

## 16. TF2

Generate TF tree:

```bash
ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames
```

Monitor transforms:

```bash
ros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo map base_link
ros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo odom base_link
```

Static transform example:

```bash
ros2 run tf2_ros static_transform_publisher \
  --x 0 \
  --y 0 \
  --z 0 \
  --roll 0 \
  --pitch 0 \
  --yaw 0 \
  --frame-id base_link \
  --child-frame-id laser
```

## 17. ROS 2 Daemon

```bash
ros2 daemon status
ros2 daemon start
ros2 daemon stop
```

Restart:

```bash
ros2 daemon stop
ros2 daemon start
```

## 18. ROS Domain ID

```bash
echo $ROS_DOMAIN_ID
export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=10
```

Persist:

```bash
echo 'export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=10' >> ~/.bashrc
```

## 19. Distribution Information

```bash
echo $ROS_DISTRO
echo $ROS_VERSION
```

## 20. Remapping

Topic:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  -r /old_topic:=/new_topic
```

Node name:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  -r __node:=robot_controller
```

Namespace:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  -r __ns:=/robot1
```

Multiple remappings:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  -r /cmd_vel:=/robot1/cmd_vel \
  -r /scan:=/robot1/scan
```

## 21. Logging

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  --log-level debug
```

Logger-specific level:

```bash
ros2 run my_package my_node \
  --ros-args \
  --log-level my_logger:=debug
```

Logs:

```bash
ls -lah ~/.ros/log
```

## 22. Common Robot Topics

```bash
ros2 topic echo /cmd_vel
ros2 topic echo /odom
ros2 topic echo /scan
ros2 topic echo /imu
ros2 topic echo /joint_states
ros2 topic echo /tf
ros2 topic echo /tf_static
ros2 topic echo /map
```

Check rates:

```bash
ros2 topic hz /scan
ros2 topic hz /odom
ros2 topic hz /joint_states
```

## 23. Robot Graph Debugging

A useful debugging sequence:

```bash
ros2 node list
ros2 topic list -t
ros2 service list -t
ros2 action list -t

ros2 node info /robot_controller
ros2 topic info /cmd_vel --verbose
ros2 topic echo /cmd_vel
ros2 topic hz /cmd_vel
```

## 24. GUI and Visualization

```bash
rqt
rqt_graph
rviz2
```

Alternatively:

```bash
ros2 run rqt_graph rqt_graph
```

## 25. Development Workflow

New terminal:

```bash
cd ~/ros_wms
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
```

After modifying code:

```bash
colcon build --symlink-install
source install/setup.bash
```

Build only `hello`:

```bash
colcon build \
  --symlink-install \
  --packages-select hello

source install/setup.bash
ros2 run hello publisher
```

## 26. Quick Debug Checklist

### Node/package cannot be found

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash

ros2 pkg list | grep <package>
ros2 pkg executables <package>
```

### Nodes cannot discover each other

```bash
echo $ROS_DOMAIN_ID
ros2 node list

ros2 daemon stop
ros2 daemon start
```

### Topic exists but no data arrives

```bash
ros2 topic info /topic --verbose
ros2 topic echo /topic
ros2 topic hz /topic
```

### Build problems

```bash
rm -rf build install log

rosdep install \
  --from-paths src \
  --ignore-src \
  -r -y

colcon build --symlink-install
```

## 27. Command Help

```bash
ros2 --help

ros2 topic --help
ros2 node --help
ros2 service --help
ros2 action --help
ros2 param --help
ros2 bag --help

ros2 topic pub --help
ros2 topic echo --help
ros2 service call --help
ros2 action send_goal --help
```

The ROS 2 CLI is extensible, so use `ros2 --help` to see all commands available on the current development machine or robot.

## Current Project Quick Start

```bash
git clone git@github.com:kofinder/ros_wms.git
cd ros_wms

source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash

rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -r -y

colcon build --symlink-install

source install/setup.bash

ros2 run hello publisher
```

